# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE, a copied sub occurrence: Box's callable field holds the sub bump, so b1, a copy of Box
# under a copy of the unit, holds bump's own occurrence there; `b1\bump()` runs that occurrence, whose body writes
# through the free input a3 by the Wide of its own node.  The call admits the root's a3 to that requirement, and the
# write lands in the root's a3 (2 + 1), its pad untouched.  HEAD refused it in every mode ("a field of a formal
# admitted by name is not carried by its value").  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
sub: bump ()
    a3\x: a3\x + 1
end: bump
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: bump
end: Box
b1: merge: Box
a3: merge: Wide
b1\bump()
int: ok 7
if: a3\x != 3 || a3\pad != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
